(A live orbit-lit torus, written in native PlainSpeak.)
(Generated by scripts/gen_donut_engine.py; do not edit by hand.)
(It is a faithful companion to the canonical doughnut.c renderer: the program computes the per-frame vertex stream — torus mesh R_MAJOR 2.0 / R_MINOR 0.8 with 50 by 30 steps, rotate_vector in X, Y, Z order, an orbiting point light advanced by 0.025 before each frame, angle Z advanced by 0.003 after it, normalized Lambertian lighting with the 0.08 ambient floor and 1/(1+0.04*dist) attenuation, and perspective projection at fov 500 and camera distance 5 — while host/donut_host.c embeds the 800x600 z-buffered Gouraud rasterizer.)
Import the C function printf taking a pointer to character and variadic parameters, returning an integer, from the header "stdio.h".
(A finite 2-frame prefix of the same animation, used by the golden and canonical-parity pipelines.)
Set az to 0.0.
Set la to 0.0.
Set caxy to 0.87758256189.
Set saxy to 0.479425538604.
For f from 1 to 2:
Add 0.025 to la.
Set lx to cosine of la times 4.5.
Set ly to sine of la times 4.5.
Set lz to sine of (la times 0.7) times 2.5.
Set caz to cosine of az.
Set saz to sine of az.
Call printf with "F\n" done.
Set i to 0.0.
While i is less than 50:
Set cu to cosine of (i times 0.125663706144).
Set su to sine of (i times 0.125663706144).
Set j to 0.0.
While j is less than 30:
Set cv to cosine of (j times 0.209439510239).
Set sv to sine of (j times 0.209439510239).
Set rad to 2.0 plus 0.8 times cv.
Set bx to rad times cu.
Set by to rad times su.
Set bz to 0.8 times sv.
Set nx to cv times cu.
Set ny to cv times su.
Set py1 to by times caxy minus bz times saxy.
Set pz1 to by times saxy plus bz times caxy.
Set px2 to bx times caxy plus pz1 times saxy.
Set pz2 to pz1 times caxy minus bx times saxy.
Set rx to px2 times caz minus py1 times saz.
Set ry to px2 times saz plus py1 times caz.
Set ny1 to ny times caxy minus sv times saxy.
Set nz1 to ny times saxy plus sv times caxy.
Set nx2 to nx times caxy plus nz1 times saxy.
Set nz2 to nz1 times caxy minus nx times saxy.
Set rnx to nx2 times caz minus ny1 times saz.
Set rny to nx2 times saz plus ny1 times caz.
Set dx to lx minus rx.
Set dy to ly minus ry.
Set dz to lz minus pz2.
Set dst to square root of (dx times dx plus dy times dy plus dz times dz).
Set dx to dx divided by dst.
Set dy to dy divided by dst.
Set dz to dz divided by dst.
Set inten to rnx times dx plus rny times dy plus nz2 times dz.
Set inten to (Choose 0.08 when inten is less than 0.08 otherwise inten) divided by (1 plus 0.04 times dst).
Set w to pz2 plus 5.0.
Set pxv to rx divided by w times 500.0 plus 400.
Set pyv to ry divided by w times 500.0 plus 300.
Call printf with "%g\n", pxv done.
Call printf with "%g\n", pyv done.
Call printf with "%g\n", w done.
Call printf with "%g\n", inten done.
Add 1.0 to j.
End while.
Add 1.0 to i.
End while.
Call printf with "S\n" done.
Add 0.003 to az.
End for.
